//
// The tail pipeline's structural gate: iron's addnorm_ffn (AN1 -> FFN with
// partial-sum staging -> AN2), ported as builders/tail_pipeline.py, ROUTED
// AS ONE SEGMENT by the production aircc.
//
// Host-only, on purpose: tail_pipeline_structure.py compiles the module
// through XRTBackend(debug_ir=True) in a temp cwd, reads the per-pass dumps
// and asserts twelve clauses (one tile-bearing device besides aircc's reset
// PDI, core->core flows exactly n_b + 2, zero packet channels, the per-column shim MM2S census with
// its negative control, the memtile and core BD caps, the L1 buffer plan
// per core, the 4-D retile living on a memtile, dispatch by symbol,
// lowering liveness, one token on every core-tile lock op, and the down
// feed's strict two-buffer alternation -- the last two read the
// 2026-08-22 deadlock and its wrong answer off the routed dump). No NPU, no
// device lock, no kernel objects: the
// compile ends at the core-ELF link, deliberately, and clause 1 requires
// that THAT be the only error. Modelled on run_ffn_resident_emulation_tests
// .lit (the arm that stays live while a device gate is parked); what it
// needs beyond that lit is aircc and the Peano linker, so a tree without
// Peano reports UNSUPPORTED rather than failing clause 1 on a different
// error text -- and the Peano root is handed to make explicitly, because
// lit sanitizes the environment and without it aiecc takes the chess path
// and fails earlier, on that other text.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for directives, so naming
// one in prose registers as a second directive. Describe them, never spell
// them out.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_tail_pipeline_structure
// RUN: cd test_tail_pipeline_structure
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-tail-pipeline-structure PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// The census's negative control FIRST: an arm that cannot fail is not a
// gate. Three herd-direct L3 streams per column must read 3 against a
// budget of 2, and the pre-widening shim->core-only count must read 0 on it.
// CHECK: census negative control: 3 L3 streams per column -> widened census 3, pre-widening shim->core count 0, packet streams 12
//
// Both verdict lines, with every count stated inside them, so a lowering
// that re-split the segment, moved a stage edge, packet-multiplexed a
// column, grew a memtile program, rotated an L1 buffer, or moved the retile
// off the memtile cannot match here. The literals are RE-DERIVED from a
// dump written by build-xrt's aircc of 2026-08-19 15:36 (sha256 254eb3ba)
// on 2026-08-22, and re-derived the same day twice (the same compiler):
// after the deadlock fix, and after the width restructure -- one down herd
// per column with its own channels and memtile, every feed get the same
// whole-buffer BD (a two-BD cycle on every down core), AN1's residual
// core->core to AN2 (two more core->core flows), the chain's last column
// forwarding its block through the accumulate kernel against a zero chunk
// (no adder at the baseline). If one has to move, re-derive it from a
// fresh dump of the compiler in hand and record that compiler -- never
// confirm it against the previous value.
//
// Baseline: iron's test.py row (64, 48, 96, m 64, k 48, n 96, depth 1,
// nB 1). Six cores in one row; ONE core->core flow (up -> down); six
// L2-staged shim streams over five columns, worst column 2; the
// row-major -> blocked retile as FOUR-dimensional memtile BDs (rpc = 32,
// four microtile rows); THREE core->core flows (one H edge, two residual
// edges); no adder (the lone column forwards its block through the
// accumulate kernel against the zero chunk); seven shim MM2S (the six
// inputs plus the zero slab); core BDs 5 = the feed's two + H + two MM2S;
// L1 53248 B = the down core's six buffers plus the stack.
// CHECK: [tail-pipeline-structure] tail_pipeline [baseline 64x48x96 m64 k48 n96 d1 nb1]: PASS (1 device, 6 cores, 3 core->core, 0 packet-typed channels, shim MM2S 7/16 worst column 2, memtile BDs max 9/48, core BDs max 5/16, L1 worst 53248 B, memtile 4-D BDs 4, adders 0, multi-token core locks 0, alternating feeds 1/1)
//
// Chain: the 16-row tile with a two-block ring and two columns, four bands
// inside the module. Eight cores; FOUR core->core flows (two H edges, two
// residual edges); the retile collapses to 3-D (rpc = 8, one microtile
// row) so the 4-D count is legitimately 0 and clause 8 only forbids a 4-D
// BD on a core there; exactly ONE down core carries the eltwise add
// (column 0 folds in column 1's block, relayed through L2; column 1
// forwards its own against the zero chunk); eight shim MM2S (x, residual,
// gamma1, w_up, gamma2, two w_down slabs, the zero slab); memtile BDs 18 on the
// AN1-input memtile (its three buffers double-buffered across the bands).
// CHECK: [tail-pipeline-structure] tail_pipeline [chain 64x96x192 m16 k48 n96 d2 nb2]: PASS (1 device, 8 cores, 4 core->core, 0 packet-typed channels, shim MM2S 8/16 worst column 2, memtile BDs max 18/48, core BDs max 5/16, L1 worst 20992 B, memtile 4-D BDs 0, adders 1, multi-token core locks 0, alternating feeds 2/2)
//
// Width: the layer's width as one band (band-serial), tile_k 192 so the ring
// is four deep (a memtile channel pair's 24 BDs hold a column's two feed
// tasks at 4*depth = 16 plus its refill), two columns, single-slot L2
// (the backend's omit_pingpong, the only form whose AN memtile fits 48).
// Memtile BDs 22 on a down column (16 feed, 4 store, refill, relay);
// core BDs 7 on the AN cores (gamma, four un-tiled blocks, the residual,
// the y store); L1 62464 B = the k-192 down core.
// CHECK: [tail-pipeline-structure] tail_pipeline [width 16x768x3072 m16 k192 n96 d4 nb2]: PASS (1 device, 8 cores, 4 core->core, 0 packet-typed channels, shim MM2S 8/16 worst column 2, memtile BDs max 22/48, core BDs max 7/16, L1 worst 62464 B, memtile 4-D BDs 0, adders 1, multi-token core locks 0, alternating feeds 2/2)
//
// The verdict last, so a clause that stops being defined fails here rather
// than passing quietly.
// CHECK: [tail-pipeline-structure] PASS
